1
00:00:00,159 --> 00:00:03,500
Here's how you protect your RV roof in under a minute, solo.

2
00:00:03,619 --> 00:00:07,839
This is an RV roof cover, sized twenty-one by ten feet.

3
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:13,219
It only covers the roof, not the whole RV—no heavy tarp to wrestle with in the wind.

4
00:00:13,359 --> 00:00:16,059
The fabric is heavy-duty 210 denier.

5
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:19,420
It holds up against rain, snow, and sun all winter long.

6
00:00:19,579 --> 00:00:22,420
You strap it down with the drawstring at the edge.

7
00:00:22,459 --> 00:00:24,879
It stays put even when the wind really kicks up.

8
00:00:24,979 --> 00:00:26,919
One person can do it alone.

9
00:00:27,019 --> 00:00:28,879
No one needs to hold the other end.

10
00:00:28,899 --> 00:00:32,639
When it's not in use, it folds into the included storage bag.

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,459
No room taken in the storage compartment.

12
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:37,840
A simple way to protect the most expensive surface on your RV.
